# Pulse tick: /dream (claude-vault Phase 4, explore-76oc §4.4) — the propose-only
# "sleep-time" learning loop. Injects `/dream tick` into the durable `dream` window;
# it's a genuine LLM tick (mines recent sessions via /recall, reasons, files
# HUMAN-GATED proposal beads — never writes MEMORY.md). Current-slug scoped (explore
# only) for confidential safety. UNJAILED by design: it reads transcript history, not
# the web, so it sits outside the untrusted-input threat the bwrap jail addresses.
#
# Renamed 2026-07-27 (explore-w1mn): pulse-recall-distill -> pulse-dream, and
# --window dive -> --window dream (its own window, per the one-window-per-loop
# scheme in ~/explore/.claude/identity.yml). ENABLED — fires weekly, see the timer.
# Unrelated to mud-distill.service (the golem MUD learning-crew dispatch).
# Inspect runs: journalctl --user -u pulse-dream.service -n 20
[Unit]
Description=Pulse tick: dream (learning loop, injected into the dream window)

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=%h/dotfiles/agents/scheduler/pulse-inject.sh --loop %p --dir %h/explore --session zig-computer --window dream --cmd "/dream tick" --launch "claude --permission-mode bypassPermissions"
